The knowledge-extraction prompts in crates/knowledge/src/extract.rs are adapted
from Kiro Crew's src/kiro_crew/knowledge/extractor.py. The DIVIXI contributors
modified them by adding a rule that the title, descriptions and summary be
written in the language of the chunk, and a rule forbidding tool use. The
search-result formatting in crates/knowledge/src/lib.rs follows Kiro Crew's
local_knowledge_search output format.

The chunking strategy, retrieval-fusion weighting, supervised SSH tunnel options
and dashboard token-auth scheme in DIVIXI were reimplemented in Rust from Kiro
Crew's published design and source. No Python source was copied for these.

DIVIXI's user interface was designed by studying Kiro Crew's. No code,
stylesheet, icon, font or image was copied.

